{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "87d8abd2-725f-4ba9-a60c-e7bb75f356fd",
    "name": "WisePlayer - Resume Playback (Watch Progress)",
    "description": "⚠️  CRITICAL NOTE FOR FRONTEND DEVELOPERS ⚠️\n\nThere is ONE and ONLY ONE endpoint for saving progress:\n  POST /api/progress\n\nDO NOT call:\n  ❌ POST /api/series/progress\n  ❌ POST /api/movie/progress\n  ❌ POST /api/vod/progress\n\nThe `streamType` field in the request body (\"VOD\" or \"SERIES\") is what tells the server which type of content you are tracking.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nHOW THE FULL FLOW WORKS:\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n1. Device registers → gets X-Device-Token\n2. User browses content:\n     - GET /api/movie  → Lists VOD categories or streams\n     - GET /api/series → Lists Series categories, series list, or episode info\n   Each stream in the response already includes a `watch_progress` object if the user has previously watched it.\n3. User plays a video:\n     - GET /api/movie?streamId=X  → returns the playback URL for a VOD\n     - GET /api/series/play?episodeId=X → returns the playback URL for a Series episode\n4. While playing, frontend calls POST /api/progress every 10-15 seconds.\n5. On pause/exit/app kill, frontend calls POST /api/progress one final time.\n6. Next time user opens the app and browses, the GET endpoints in step 2 will return the saved `resume_position_seconds` automatically.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "53194675"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "── STEP 1: Device Setup ──",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register Device → Get Token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Device registered successfully', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 201]);",
                  "    pm.expect(json.token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});",
                  "if (json.token) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('deviceToken', json.token);",
                  "    console.log('✅ deviceToken saved:', json.token);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"deviceId\": \"{{deviceFingerprint}}\",\n  \"deviceModel\": \"Postman\",\n  \"osVersion\": \"1.0\",\n  \"platform\": \"postman\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/device/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "device",
                "register"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "── STEP 2: Save Progress (POST /api/progress) ──",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "✅ Save Progress - VOD (Correct URL)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Progress saved (200)', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200));",
                  "pm.test('Response has resume_position_seconds', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('resume_position_seconds');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Response has fully_watched flag', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('fully_watched');",
                  "});",
                  "console.log('📼 VOD progress saved. fully_watched:', json.fully_watched, '| resume_position_seconds:', json.resume_position_seconds);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "packages": {},
                "requests": {}
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Device-Token",
                "value": "{{deviceToken}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Device-Fingerprint",
                "value": "{{deviceFingerprint}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"playlistId\": \"{{playlistId}}\",\n  \"streamId\": {{vodStreamId}},\n  \"streamType\": \"VOD\",\n  \"positionSeconds\": 180,\n  \"durationSeconds\": 7200\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/progress",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "progress"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
